  ["kototama.tender's host-import module name was wrongly \"kototama\" -- fixed to \"kotoba\" (kotoba.runtime's WASM encoder hardcodes this for every real compiled guest; the WAT test fixtures only ever passed against themselves, never a real compiled guest)"
   "aiueos.execute/launcher (JVM-only, found already implementing a similar Chicory-hosted capability-gated execution idea under aiueos's own manifest/broker vocabulary) is NOT adopted as a kototama.tender replacement -- consolidation on the JVM substrate is deliberately deferred, not decided here"
   "kototama.contract's actor:host ABI lands on the BROWSER-native substrate first (actor-host.js in kotoba-lang/wasm-webcomponent, plain JS matching that repo's existing zero-build-step convention), per the owner's .cljc runtime priority (kototama > cljs > nbb > jvm) -- only 4 of 8 imports (now/sha256-hex/log-read/log-append!) are implemented, since gen-keypair/sign/verify/http-post need an async Web Crypto/fetch call a synchronous Wasm host import can't perform"
   "kototama's web/index.html is now generated via kotoba-lang/html + kotoba-lang/css (Hiccup EDN -> HTML/CSS) run under nbb (generate.cljs), applying the same .cljc priority rule to authoring the page itself, not just guest-side logic"]
